(project tuna-metatheory
  (doc "Tuna book chapter: metatheory - the proof ladder. Pre-registered as a sketch so the substrate never grows a feature that forecloses it. Thesis: replay verification, derivation recording, and machine-checked metatheory are one ladder, not three projects; each rung makes the next mechanical. Agreed with roerick 2026-10-19.")
  (* agent note (|2026-10-19, THE LADDER (agreed with roerick):
      RUNG 1 - REPLAY VERIFICATION (live): determinism is a tested invariant
      (SPEC section 2); a run is machine-checked by re-execution - input
      hash -> output hash, same step count. Verifies THIS execution only;
      no universal claim.
      RUNG 2 - DERIVATION RECORDING (the provable-backend gap, parked
      09-19; next milestone after FED3): journals hold boundary events only
      today; record the reduction sequence so a derivation V0 ->* V1
      becomes a machine-checkable equational proof of V0 = V1 - every step
      is one of the five rules, replay verifies each step. Unlocks
      postmortem-as-proof (the SWARM-1 journal format) and factory
      write-back receipts.
      RUNG 3 - COQ/Rocq FORMALIZATION OF THE CORE (carded on PP 10-19):
      five rules as an inductive reduction relation; theorems - determinism
      (unique reduct) and values-closed-under-reduction (a program applied
      to data either diverges or yields data; the receipt soundness
      theorem); extract an OCaml evaluator from the proved definition;
      differential bench vs the validated step-counting CL reference
      (~/tree-calc/tree-calc.lisp) over a bench battery - same input tree,
      same result, same step count, all three engines. Deliverable: a
      certified canonical engine - F1 canonical side made unimpeachable
      (the optimized engine must match it or the engine split stands, per
      acceptance.borg F1). Step 0: survey existing formalizations
      (barry-jay-personal/tree-calculus book + blog, olydis/tree-calculus,
      treecalcul.us; web.search down 10-19, gist + curl reachable). What
      Coq does NOT give: proofs about particular runs (rung 2 is the tool)
      and the typed layer (rung 4 is a separate development).
      RUNG 4 - TYPED LAYER (Jay typed/delta calculus; roerick: types are
      just functions): types live ABOVE the five rules, never as new core
      rules. A type is a tree-valued function; a type check is a reduction
      (apply the value to its type, reduce to true); the checker is a
      tree-calculus program in the store, journaled and replayable -
      well-typed becomes a claim with a receipt. Adopting Jay typed
      semantics as new core rules would re-derive the whole book - rejected
      for v0. Checker runs under the fuel/size budget, canonical step
      accounting (F1).
      RUNG 5 - PROOF TERMS: propositions as trees, proof terms as trees
      (derivation chains + lemmas), checker = a tree-calculus program.
      Where rungs 4 and 5 merge: a type judgment is a reduction, a proof
      is a derivation, both are receipts from the same journal.
      WALL - META-THEOREMS stay in the book as hand-argued chapters + tests
      (or a host prover): termination, checker totality, for-all-inputs
      safety cannot be proven by the engine about itself (Turing-complete;
      treecalcul.us demos the halting problem). We do not build a proof
      kernel inside tuna. Independent-verifier note: promoting the CL
      reference to a second implementation cross-checking the OCaml engine
      is the cheap trust story and needs no proof language.|) *)
  (status sketch))
